To properly process link-bandwidth extended communities from multiple EBGP neighbors in your IPv6 multihoming deployment, configure the following on your Nokia router:

1. First, enter the BGP group or neighbor link-bandwidth configuration context:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> link-bandwidth
```

2. Enable acceptance of link-bandwidth communities from EBGP peers for IPv6 routes:
```
accept-from-ebgp ipv6
```

3. Optionally, if you want to automatically add link-bandwidth communities to received EBGP routes:
```
add-to-received-ebgp ipv6
```

4. If you need to aggregate bandwidth values from multiple paths:
```
aggregate-used-paths ipv6
```

5. To send link-bandwidth communities to EBGP peers when advertising routes:
```
send-to-ebgp ipv6
```

These commands will ensure proper interpretation and application of link-bandwidth metrics in your route selection logic. The exact combination depends on whether you're configuring at the group or neighbor level, and your specific traffic engineering requirements.
