To enable proper utilization of the link-bandwidth attribute from external BGP peers while maintaining backward compatibility, configure the following commands under your BGP group or neighbor context:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
```

If you need to automatically add link-bandwidth to routes received from directly connected EBGP peers, also include:
```
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
```

These commands will:
1. Accept and process link-bandwidth attributes from EBGP peers for IPv4 routes
2. Send link-bandwidth attributes to EBGP peers when advertising IPv4 routes
3. Aggregate bandwidth values from multipath routes when readvertising with next-hop-self
4. (Optional) Automatically add link-bandwidth to routes from single-hop EBGP peers

The configuration maintains backward compatibility as these features only affect routes where the address family is explicitly specified (IPv4 in this case).
