## Proposed answer:
To enable dynamic acceptance of ORF entries via extended communities during BGP peering session upgrades without disrupting existing policy, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        outbound-route-filtering
            extended-community
                accept-orf
                send-orf
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<peer-group-name>` with your specific BGP peer group name. This configuration:
1. Enables the router to accept ORF entries from the peer (`accept-orf`)
2. Negotiates the ability to send ORF entries to the peer (`send-orf`)
3. Operates at the extended community level for selective route filtering

For dynamic neighbors, you may also want to set appropriate limits if needed:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        dynamic-neighbor-limit <max-peers>
        exit
    exit
```
Where `<max-peers>` is your desired maximum number of dynamic sessions.
