To dynamically append link-bandwidth extended communities to all IPv4 prefixes learned via EBGP adjacencies without manual per-route intervention, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This configuration will:
1. Automatically add link-bandwidth communities to all received IPv4 routes from directly connected EBGP peers
2. Allow sending these communities to other EBGP peers
3. Accept and use the bandwidth values from received communities
4. Aggregate bandwidth values when readvertising routes with next-hop-self
---
