Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
Here are the recommended CLI configurations for your Nokia routers to ensure proper propagation of VPNv4 prefixes and labeled IPv6 routes via BGP peers while maintaining IPv6 next-hop reachability over an IPv6-only underlay:

```cli
# Enable extended next-hop encoding capabilities for VPNv4 and labeled IPv4
configure router bgp
    extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4 label-ipv4
exit

# Configure BGP to advertise IPv6 next-hops for VPNv4, VPNv6, labeled IPv4, and labeled IPv6 routes
configure router bgp
    advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6 label-ipv4 label-ipv6
exit

# Configure next-hop resolution for labeled and VPN routes
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel
    family vpn
    exit
    family label-ipv6
    exit
exit

# Enable BGP fast reroute for critical address families
configure router bgp
    backup-path label-ipv4 label-ipv6
exit

# Configure address families for BGP peers (example for a specific neighbor)
configure router bgp group <GROUP_NAME> neighbor <NEIGHBOR_IP>
    family vpn-ipv4
    family vpn-ipv6
    family label-ipv6
exit
```

These configurations will:
1. Enable extended next-hop encoding capabilities required for IPv6 next-hops with IPv4 routes
2. Ensure proper advertisement of IPv6 next-hops across all relevant route types
3. Set up next-hop resolution for labeled and VPN routes
4. Provide fast reroute protection for labeled routes
5. Activate the necessary address families for BGP peers
