To ensure locally originated /32 LDP FECs are consistently advertised via BGP with RFC 3107 labels during your RSVP-TE to LDP-BGP migration, configure the following:

1. Enable LDP prefix advertisement for BGP neighbors:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> advertise-ldp-prefix
```

2. Configure the resolution filter to prioritize LDP for next-hop resolution:
```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunnel family ipv4 resolution-filter ldp
```

3. Optionally disable RSVP if it should no longer be used:
```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunnel family ipv4 resolution-filter no rsvp
```

These commands will ensure your local /32 LDP FECs are advertised via BGP-LU (RFC 3107) regardless of existing BGP paths in the RIB.
