To ensure consistent propagation of LLGR-stale routes during your BGP migration to a new AS, configure the following on your Nokia routers:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            forwarding-bits-set all
            advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors without-no-export
        exit
    exit
```

For eBGP peers that will exit your current AS, also consider adding these configurations to maintain stability during the transition:

```
configure router bgp
    enforce-first-as
    best-path-selection
        ignore-router-id
    exit
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Set the F-bit for all AFI/SAFIs to indicate preserved forwarding state
2. Allow LLGR stale routes to be advertised to all peers (including those without LLGR capability)
3. Permit these routes to exit your AS via the `without-no-export` option
4. Maintain routing stability during AS migration by relaxing some path selection criteria
