        exit
    exit
exit
```

Key points:
- `advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors` enables propagation to legacy peers without LLGR support
- Omit `without-no-export` to maintain the no-export policy for routes leaving your AS
- `forwarding-bits-set all` ensures proper F-bit signaling for all address families
- The helper stale-time values can be adjusted based on your migration requirements

For specific peer groups or neighbors where you need different behavior, apply these configurations at the group or neighbor level under their respective graceful-restart contexts.
