To ensure stale routes persist for 24 hours (86,400 seconds) during BGP graceful restarts, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        stale-routes-time 86400
        long-lived
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Sets the stale route retention period to 86,400 seconds (24 hours)
2. Enables Long-Lived Graceful Restart (LLGR) capabilities

Note that the `stale-routes-time` parameter accepts values up to 3,600 seconds by default. For 24-hour persistence, you'll need to verify if your platform supports extended timer values beyond the documented maximum. If not, you may need to implement alternative solutions such as scripted route preservation.
