To achieve proper load balancing for IPv4 prefixes advertised via BGP with next-hop-self while aggregating bandwidth metrics from link-bandwidth extended communities across ECMP paths, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
            exit
        next-hop-self
        exit
```

If you need to automatically add link-bandwidth extended communities to routes received from directly connected EBGP peers, include this additional command under the `link-bandwidth` context:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
            exit
        next-hop-self
        exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name. This configuration ensures proper aggregation of bandwidth metrics for IPv4 prefixes while maintaining next-hop-self behavior.
