To maintain uniform AS path attributes when aggregating routes across all nodes in your autonomous system during a multi-site BGP deployment, use the following CLI configuration commands:

1. Enable `aggregator-id-zero` to ensure consistent AS path attributes in aggregated routes:
```cli
configure router bgp
    aggregator-id-zero
exit
```

2. Configure `aggregate-used-paths` for relevant address families to properly handle bandwidth aggregation:
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> link-bandwidth
    aggregate-used-paths ipv4
exit
```

3. Optionally enable `ibgp-multipath` if you want to load-balance traffic across multiple IBGP paths:
```cli
configure router bgp
    ibgp-multipath
exit
```

These configurations will help prevent inconsistencies in path advertisement by ensuring all nodes in your AS handle route aggregation with uniform AS path attributes.
