To optimize BGP best-path selection by leveraging IGP cost metrics while maintaining policy consistency across AS boundaries in your multi-domain MPLS VPN deployment, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    enable-inter-as-vpn
    multipath 8 ebgp 8 ibgp 8 restrict same-neighbor-as
exit

configure router bgp best-path-selection
    as-path-ignore vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6
    ebgp-ibgp-equal vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6
    ignore-router-id
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables inter-AS VPN connectivity (`enable-inter-as-vpn`)
2. Configures multipath with equal preference for EBGP/IBGP paths (`multipath` with `same-neighbor-as` restriction)
3. Ignores AS path length for VPN routes (`as-path-ignore`)
4. Treats EBGP and IBGP paths equally (`ebgp-ibgp-equal`)
5. Disables router ID comparison (`ignore-router-id`)

These settings allow the IGP metrics to play a greater role in path selection while maintaining consistent routing policies across AS boundaries.
