To ensure your Nokia router correctly resolves BGP next-hops for labeled and VPN prefixes via static routing while preventing default static routes from interfering, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            allow-static
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        static
                    exit
                exit
                family vpn
                    resolution-filter
                        static
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

### Key Points:
1. **`allow-static`** enables static route resolution for BGP next-hops but excludes default routes (`0/0`, `::/0`).
2. **`resolution-filter static`** explicitly restricts next-hop resolution to static routes for both labeled-IPv4 and VPN families.
3. This ensures only non-default static routes are used for resolving BGP next-hops in the MPLS VPN upgrade scenario.

For Route Reflector (RR) scenarios where VPN route forwarding is needed, also add:
```cli
configure router bgp
    enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
exit
```
