## User question:
"During a multi-vendor network migration where we're integrating Nokia routers into our existing BGP topology, what’s the recommended approach for configuring path selection logic when evaluating routes received from disparate autonomous systems, particularly if some peers omit the MED attribute—should those routes default to the maximum MED value for consistent decision-making?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To address your requirement for consistent path selection when dealing with routes that may omit the MED attribute, here are the recommended CLI configurations:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        deterministic-med
        always-compare-med infinity
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables `deterministic-med` to ensure consistent MED comparisons across routes from different ASes
2. Configures `always-compare-med infinity` to treat routes without MED attributes as having the maximum possible value (making them least preferred)

For completeness, you may also want to set explicit MED values for outbound advertisements:

```
configure router bgp group <PEER_GROUP_NAME>
    med-out igp-cost
exit
```

These settings will provide predictable path selection behavior during your multi-vendor migration, particularly when handling routes from peers that don't send MED values.
