## User question:
"During a multi-vendor IPv6-labeled unicast deployment, our Nokia routers appear to prioritize shorter AS paths over preferred transit links—how can we modify the BGP route selection process to disregard AS-path length while maintaining label distribution integrity?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To modify the BGP route selection process to disregard AS-path length for IPv6-labeled unicast routes while maintaining label distribution integrity, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp best-path-selection
    as-path-ignore label-ipv6
exit
```

This command specifically targets labeled IPv6 unicast routes (AFI=2, SAFI=4) and removes AS-path length from the best-path selection criteria while preserving all other aspects of label distribution and route processing.
