---
## Proposed answer:
To enable MD5 authentication for BGP peers on your Nokia 7750 SR platform using the pre-configured keychain 'secure_bgp123', follow these CLI configuration commands:

1. **Configure BGP group level authentication**:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    auth-keychain secure_bgp123
exit
```

2. **Alternatively, configure authentication for a specific neighbor**:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    auth-keychain secure_bgp123
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the specific neighbor IP if applying to individual peers. This will apply MD5 authentication to the BGP sessions using the specified keychain.
