Here are the CLI commands to configure MD5 authentication with the pre-shared key 'SecureKey123!' using the hash2 algorithm on your Nokia routers:

```
configure router bgp
    group <your-group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip-address>
            authentication-key "SecureKey123!" hash2
```

Replace `<your-group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ip-address>` with the IP address of your BGP neighbor. This configuration must be applied to both ends of the BGP peering session with the same key to establish connectivity.

For enhanced security, consider implementing these additional best practices:
```
configure router bgp
    group <your-group-name>
        enforce-first-as
        prefix-limit ipv4 <appropriate-limit-value> threshold 75 idle-timeout 15
```
