Here are the CLI configuration commands to implement BGP peering with ASN 65001 as your local autonomous system on a Nokia (Alcatel-Lucent) service router:

```cli
configure router
    autonomous-system 65001
    bgp
        enforce-first-as
        exit
    exit
```

If you need to configure specific BGP groups or neighbors with additional parameters (like peer AS, passive mode, or local-as options), here are examples of those commands:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group "PEER_GROUP_NAME"
            peer-as <REMOTE_AS_NUMBER>
            passive
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

For inter-AS VPN connectivity (if required):
```cli
configure router
    bgp
        enable-inter-as-vpn
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `PEER_GROUP_NAME` with your BGP group name and `<REMOTE_AS_NUMBER>` with the actual remote AS number. Adjust other parameters (like passive mode) based on your specific peering requirements.
