To achieve sub-second path switchover for labeled-IPv6 BGP prefixes during primary MPLS link failure while maintaining existing policy controls, implement the following configurations:

1. Enable BGP Fast Reroute for labeled-IPv6 routes:
```
configure router bgp
    backup-path label-ipv6
exit
```

2. Configure add-paths for multicast VPN IPv6 routes to ensure multiple paths are available:
```
configure router bgp group <group_name> neighbor <neighbor_ip> family vpn-ipv6
    add-paths mvpn-ipv6 send 2 receive
exit
```

3. For next-hop resolution optimization:
```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family label-ipv6
    resolution-filter
        ldp
        rsvp
    exit
exit
```

These commands will enable:
- Pre-computed backup paths for rapid failover
- Multiple path advertisement/reception for redundancy
- Optimized next-hop resolution over both LDP and RSVP tunnels

The combination ensures sub-second convergence while preserving existing routing policies.
