To achieve sub-second convergence for labeled unicast IPv6 prefixes during primary link failures, implement the following BGP-LU configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    backup-path label-ipv6
    graceful-restart
    add-paths
        label-ipv6 send 8 receive
    exit
```

Key elements of this configuration:
1. Enables BGP Fast Reroute specifically for labeled IPv6 routes (`backup-path label-ipv6`)
2. Activates Graceful Restart to maintain forwarding during control plane transitions
3. Configures Add-Paths capability to allow receiving and advertising multiple paths for labeled IPv6 prefixes

For optimal route reflection, you should also configure reference locations with their primary IPv6 addresses:
```
configure router bgp orr location <LOCATION_NAME>
    primary-ipv6-address <IPV6_ADDRESS>
exit
```
