To adjust BGP route preferences on your Nokia 7750 SR, use the following CLI sequence to access the appropriate configuration context and modify the path attributes:

1. Enter the BGP configuration context:
   ```
   configure router bgp
   ```

2. Depending on where you want to apply the preference (global BGP, group, or neighbor level), navigate to the desired context:
   - For global BGP settings:
     ```
     preference <value>
     ```
   - For a specific BGP group:
     ```
     group <group-name>
     preference <value>
     ```
   - For a specific neighbor within a group:
     ```
     group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
     preference <value>
     ```

Replace `<value>` with your desired preference (1 to 255). The default is 170 if not specified. 

Example for setting a global preference of 100:
```
configure router bgp
preference 100
exit all
```
