To dynamically stabilize BGP sessions influenced by underlying link-state verification, configure the following:

```
configure router bgp
    damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 10 15 120 error-interval 20
    hold-time 180 min 60
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Implements progressive damping for unstable peers (starting at 10 minutes, doubling to 15 minutes, capping at 120 minutes)
2. Requires 20 minutes of stable operation to reset the oscillation penalty
3. Enforces a 180-second hold timer with a minimum acceptable value of 60 seconds

For critical peers where immediate updates are required after session establishment, add:
```
configure router bgp group <group_name> neighbor <ip_address>
    initial-send-delay-zero
exit
```
