To minimize route flapping during your BGP peer migration to redundant links on the Nokia 7750 SR platform, implement the following configuration:

```cli
# Enable immediate BGP updates when sessions establish
configure router bgp
    initial-send-delay-zero
exit

# Configure BGP peer tracking for faster convergence
configure router bgp
    enable-peer-tracking
exit

# Enable BGP graceful restart to maintain routes during transitions
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
exit

# Set up backup paths for fast reroute capability
configure router bgp
    backup-path ipv4 ipv6 label-ipv4 label-ipv6
exit

# Optionally leverage Segment Routing policies for next-hop resolution
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunn family ipv4 resolution-filter
    sr-policy
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Send updates immediately when BGP sessions come up
2. Accelerate peer failure detection by tracking interface/routing changes
3. Maintain routing continuity during session resets
4. Pre-compute backup paths for rapid failover
5. Use SR policies (if deployed) for additional path redundancy
------------
