Here are the CLI configuration commands to implement BGP route reflectors with ORR capabilities and ensure local prefix reachability:

```
configure router bgp
    cluster 10.20.30.40 orr-location 5 allow-local-fallback
    location 5
    backup-path ipv4
    optimal-route-reflection
        location 5
    exit
    next-hop-resolution labeled-routes
        rr-use-route-table
    exit
exit
```

Key features implemented:
- Configured cluster ID 10.20.30.40 with ORR location 5
- Enabled local fallback routes when optimal paths are unavailable (`allow-local-fallback`)
- Set up backup path calculation for IPv4 prefixes
- Configured route table lookups for labeled routes resolution
- Established optimal route reflection with location ID 5

The configuration ensures your route reflector will:
1. Advertise optimal paths based on location 5
2. Fall back to locally available routes when optimal paths become unavailable
3. Maintain reachability during path failures through pre-computed backup paths
4. Properly resolve next-hops for labeled routes
