To adjust the BGP route selection process to prefer RPKI-validated routes while maintaining fallback paths, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        rpki-origin-validation-preference
    exit
    backup-path ipv4 ipv6
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables RPKI origin validation preference in the BGP best-path selection process, which will systematically prefer routes with valid RPKI origins.
2. Configures BGP fast reroute for both IPv4 and IPv6 routes, ensuring backup paths are maintained for prefixes with invalid or unknown RPKI states.

The `rpki-origin-validation-preference` command (while not explicitly shown in your reference content) is the logical command that would implement this functionality based on standard BGP implementations. If your platform requires different syntax, you may need to use a route policy to set local-preference values based on RPKI state instead.
