Here are the CLI configuration commands to define AS 65001 and 65002 as member ASes within confederation 65100 while maintaining existing peer relationships:

```cli
configure router
    autonomous-system 65100
    confederation 65100 members 65001 65002
exit

configure router bgp
    enforce-first-as
exit
```

For existing BGP peers outside the confederation, maintain their current `peer-as` configurations. For peers within the confederation (65001 or 65002), use the following structure:

```cli
configure router bgp group INTERNAL_CONFED
    peer-as 65001
    local-as 65001 private no-prepend-global-as
exit
```

Repeat similar configurations for other internal confederation peers as needed, adjusting the `peer-as` and `local-as` values accordingly.
