## User question:
"During a recent BGP monitoring protocol (BMP) deployment on our Nokia 7750 routers, we've observed persistent session establishment failures—what would be the optimal method to implement a 30-second retry timer for reconnection attempts while maintaining stability in the existing routing infrastructure?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To implement a 30-second retry timer for BMP session reconnection attempts while maintaining stability, use the following CLI command:

```
configure bmp station "station-name" connection connect-retry 30
```

For BGP sessions, if you also want to adjust the BGP-specific connect-retry timer (though this wasn't specifically requested), you could use:
```
configure router bgp group "group-name" neighbor "ip-address" connect-retry 30
```

These configurations will set the retry timers to 30 seconds without affecting other stability parameters in your routing infrastructure.
