"During a maintenance window where we're implementing BGP dampening policies on our Nokia routers to mitigate route flapping, what's the proper way to adjust the hold-down timers so that initial stable sessions remain idle for 15 minutes post-convergence, progressively increase the backoff interval to 10 minutes upon repeated instability events with a ceiling of 120 minutes, while mandating 45 consecutive minutes of uninterrupted operation before clearing the flap penalties?"
