## Proposed answer:
Here's the CLI configuration command to implement your BGP dampening requirements:

```
configure router bgp
    damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 15 10 120 error-interval 45
exit
```

This configuration:
- Sets initial stable session idle time (`initial-wait`) to 15 minutes
- Configures progressive backoff interval (`second-wait`) to 10 minutes 
- Defines maximum penalty ceiling (`max-wait`) at 120 minutes
- Requires 45 consecutive error-free minutes (`error-interval`) to clear penalties

The command should be applied under the appropriate BGP context (global, group, or neighbor level) depending on where you want the policy enforced.
