To selectively advertise the default route to specific BGP peers within a peer group on your Nokia 7750 SR, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
# Configure the BGP peer group
configure router bgp
    group "SELECTIVE_DEFAULT_PEERS"
        family ipv4
        default-route-target
        exit
    exit

# Apply the peer group to designated neighbors
configure router bgp
    neighbor <IP_ADDRESS_OF_PEER_1>
        group "SELECTIVE_DEFAULT_PEERS"
    exit
    neighbor <IP_ADDRESS_OF_PEER_2>
        group "SELECTIVE_DEFAULT_PEERS"
    exit
```

Replace `<IP_ADDRESS_OF_PEER_1>` and `<IP_ADDRESS_OF_PEER_2>` with the actual IP addresses of your designated BGP peers. The `default-route-target` command ensures only peers in this group receive the default route advertisement. Other neighbor sessions outside this group will not be affected.
