To ensure deterministic path selection when MED attributes from disparate autonomous systems introduce ambiguity in route preference, use the following BGP configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        deterministic-med
        always-compare-med zero
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables `deterministic-med` to group paths by neighbor AS before MED comparison
2. Configures `always-compare-med zero` to allow MED comparison across different ASes while treating missing MED values as 0

For additional stability during migration, you may also consider:

```cli
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ignore-router-id
    exit
exit
```

This prevents unnecessary best-path changes due to router-ID comparisons when paths are otherwise equivalent.
