To enforce strict validation preventing peers from advertising paths with extended AS numbers while maintaining backward interoperability in SR OS, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    disable-4byte-asn
    enforce-first-as
exit
```

For specific BGP groups or neighbors that require different behavior:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    disable-4byte-asn
    enforce-first-as
exit

configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    disable-4byte-asn
    enforce-first-as
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Disable 4-byte ASN support globally or per peer/group
2. Enforce validation that the first AS in the AS_PATH matches the peer's AS number
3. Reject any updates containing 4-byte AS_PATH segments while maintaining compatibility with legacy BGP speakers
