To configure a BGP session on a Nokia router that restricts peer negotiation to IPv4 prefixes and disables all optional parameter advertisements, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        disable-capability-negotiation
        disable-4byte-asn
        no extended-nh-encoding
        family ipv4
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            prefix-limit ipv4 <max-routes>
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>`, `<peer-ip-address>`, and `<max-routes>` with your specific values. This configuration:
- Disables capability negotiation to restrict the session to IPv4 routing exchanges
- Disables 4-byte ASN support
- Explicitly turns off extended next-hop encoding capabilities
- Enables only IPv4 address family
- Sets a prefix limit for IPv4 routes
