To prevent your Nokia NRCs from propagating learned routes back to designated client peers within a targeted autonomous system block during the BGP peering migration, use the following configuration:

1. **Disable route reflection to specific clients**:
   ```
   configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <client-IP> disable-client-reflect
   ```

2. **Enable loop detection to discard routes with loops in the AS path** (optional, for additional protection):
   ```
   configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <client-IP> loop-detect discard-route
   ```

3. **Apply these settings at the group level if multiple clients share the same behavior**:
   ```
   configure router bgp group <group-name> disable-client-reflect
   configure router bgp group <group-name> loop-detect discard-route
   ```

These commands ensure routes learned from clients are not reflected back to them while maintaining the peering session. Adjust `<group-name>` and `<client-IP>` as needed for your deployment.
