To modify your Nokia router's export policy to filter out large community attributes while preserving standard ones during BGP peering with a partner AS, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip>
    disable-communities large
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ip>` with the IP address of the partner AS neighbor. This command will remove large communities from being sent to the specified peer while allowing standard communities to pass through.
