To temporarily retain BGP-learned routes after the physical interface goes down during your transit link decommissioning, configure the following commands:

```
configure router bgp
    purge-timer 30
    no enable-peer-tracking
    mp-bgp-keep
exit
```

These settings will:
1. Extend the purge timer to 30 minutes (adjustable between 1-60 minutes)
2. Disable immediate peer tracking to prevent rapid route withdrawal
3. Enable MP-BGP route retention

For additional resilience during the transition, consider enabling BGP fast reroute:

```
configure router bgp
    backup-path ipv4
exit
``` 

This will maintain IPv4 traffic flow by using pre-computed backup paths if available.
------------
