"During a maintenance window where we're decommissioning an old link, what's the recommended approach on Nokia routers to ensure BGP gracefully handles an interface failure without abruptly tearing down the external peering session?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure BGP gracefully handles an interface failure during link decommissioning without abruptly tearing down the external peering session, configure the following:

```cli
configure router bgp
    disable-fast-external-failover
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
    exit
```

For additional stability, consider adjusting the purge timer for stale routes:
```cli
configure router bgp
    purge-timer 30
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Disable immediate session teardown on interface failure (`disable-fast-external-failover`)
2. Enable long-lived graceful restart capabilities to maintain routes during transient failures
3. Extend the purge timer for stale routes to 30 minutes (default is 10), giving more time for recovery
