```
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            family ipv4
                prefix-limit ipv4 1 log-only
```

For IPv6:
```
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            family ipv6
                prefix-limit ipv6 1 log-only
```

These configurations will:
1. Maintain BGP sessions with peers
2. Accept but not install any received prefixes (by setting limit=1)
3. Generate log messages when prefixes are received (via log-only parameter)
4. Not disrupt existing adjacencies

Apply these settings to all relevant BGP neighbors participating in the phased migration. The actual forwarding table won't receive any dynamic prefixes, but all BGP monitoring capabilities remain intact.
