To dynamically establish BGP peer sessions within a predefined IP address block on a Nokia router, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        type external
        peer-as <REMOTE_AS_NUMBER>
        dynamic-neighbor
            prefix <IP_PREFIX/PREFIX_LENGTH>
        exit
        dynamic-neighbor-limit <MAX_DYNAMIC_PEERS>
    exit
exit
```

Replace:
- `<REMOTE_AS_NUMBER>` with the autonomous system number of your BGP peers
- `<IP_PREFIX/PREFIX_LENGTH>` with your predefined IP address block (e.g., 192.168.0.0/16)
- `<MAX_DYNAMIC_PEERS>` with the maximum number of simultaneous dynamic peers you want to allow

Optionally, you can add prefix limits for security:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        prefix-limit ipv4 <MAX_ROUTES> threshold 75 idle-timeout 30
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<MAX_ROUTES>` with the maximum number of routes you'll accept from each peer.
