To automate BGP peering adjustments for a predefined peer group in your Nokia-based infrastructure, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "PEER_GROUP_NAME"
        dynamic-neighbor
            prefix <ip-prefix/prefix-length>
        exit
        dynamic-neighbor-limit <peers>
        enforce-first-as
        prefix-limit <family> <limit> [threshold <percentage>] [idle-timeout <minutes>|forever|log-only] [post-import]
exit
```

Replace placeholders (`PEER_GROUP_NAME`, `ip-prefix/prefix-length`, `peers`, `family`, `limit`, etc.) with your specific values. This configuration:
1. Enables dynamic BGP sessions for the peer group
2. Defines the prefix range for acceptable dynamic peers
3. Sets a maximum number of dynamic peers
4. Enforces first AS validation
5. Configures prefix limits with optional thresholds and actions

For multiple routers, script these commands with variable substitution for group names, prefixes, and limits, then deploy during your maintenance window.
