To ensure consistent path selection between EBGP and IBGP-labeled routes during best-path calculation, configure the following commands:

```
configure router bgp
    ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv6
    exit
```

For additional optimization and redundancy, consider these complementary configurations:
```
configure router bgp
    ibgp-multipath
    backup-path label-ipv6
    next-hop-resolution labeled-routes
        allow-static
        exit
    best-path-selection
        ignore-router-id
        exit
    exit
```

These commands will:
1. Treat EBGP and IBGP-labeled IPv6 routes equally in best-path selection
2. Enable IBGP multipath load balancing
3. Configure BGP fast reroute for labeled IPv6 routes
4. Allow static routes for next-hop resolution of labeled routes
5. Ignore router ID in best-path comparisons
