"During a planned maintenance window where we're upgrading multiple Nokia routers in a core network, what’s the recommended approach for enabling BGP graceful restart to ensure uninterrupted session re-establishment if peers unexpectedly send NOTIFICATION messages due to transient faults?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP graceful restart with support for NOTIFICATION messages during your maintenance window, use these CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        enable-notification
    exit
```

For additional stability during transient faults, consider adding these complementary configurations:
```
configure router bgp
    damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 10 15 120 error-interval 45
    enable-peer-tracking
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Enable graceful restart with NOTIFICATION message support
2. Configure dampening of peer oscillations with progressive timers (10/15/120 minutes)
3. Enable faster convergence through peer tracking

Apply these at either the global BGP level or specific group/neighbor levels depending on your deployment requirements.
