To ensure your Nokia routers properly signal graceful restart capability in NOTIFICATION messages during BGP peer reconnection after a transient failure, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        enable-notification
        restart-time 120
        stale-routes-time 600
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables BGP graceful restart globally (`graceful-restart`)
2. Signals NOTIFICATION message support (`enable-notification`)
3. Sets a conservative restart timer of 120 seconds (`restart-time`)
4. Maintains stale routes for 10 minutes (600 seconds) during convergence (`stale-routes-time`)

Apply these settings under specific BGP groups or neighbors if you need granular control per peer.
