To enforce proper origin validation for labeled IPv6 routes from your trusted peer while maintaining existing MPLS transport, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
# Configure BGP group/neighbor to enable origin validation for labeled IPv6 routes
configure router bgp group <peer-group-name>
    neighbor <peer-ip-address>
        enable-origin-validation label-ipv6
exit all

# Enable comparison of origin validation states in best path selection
configure router bgp best-path-selection
    compare-origin-validation-state
exit all
```

If you also want to explicitly verify the peer's capability to send labeled routes (though this is typically auto-negotiated), add:
```cli
configure router bgp group <peer-group-name>
    extended-nh-encoding
exit all
```
