To expedite BGP path recalculation during link failures with flapping transit interfaces, implement these Nokia-specific mechanisms:

```
configure router bgp
    rapid-withdrawal
    backup-path ipv4 ipv6
    enable-peer-tracking
    graceful-restart
        stale-routes-time 300
    exit
    group <PEER_GROUP_NAME>
        hold-time 30 min 15
    exit
```

Key optimizations:
1. `rapid-withdrawal` eliminates update packing delays for immediate withdrawal propagation
2. `backup-path` pre-computes alternate paths for fast failover
3. `enable-peer-tracking` provides immediate session teardown when next-hop becomes unreachable
4. Reduced `hold-time` (30s) with minimum acceptable threshold (15s) for faster failure detection
5. Graceful restart with `stale-routes-time` maintains routes during transient failures

For critical peers, apply these settings at either the global BGP level or specific neighbor/group levels as needed.
