To expedite BGP route reconvergence during peer decommissioning with minimal disruption, apply these CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    rapid-withdrawal
    enable-peer-tracking
    purge-timer 5
exit

configure router bgp graceful-restart
    no stale-routes-time
exit
```

For immediate session teardown, also adjust the hold-time on the specific peer being decommissioned:
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <peer-ip>
    hold-time 0
exit
```

These changes will:
1. Send withdrawals immediately without delay (`rapid-withdrawal`)
2. Drop the peer instantly when its route becomes unreachable (`enable-peer-tracking`) 
3. Purge stale routes faster (`purge-timer 5`)
4. Disable stale route retention during restart (`no stale-routes-time`)
5. Force immediate session termination for the target peer (`hold-time 0`)
