To ensure all VPN-IPv4 routes are imported into a dummy VRF instance for BGP next-hop resolution while bypassing standard RT-based filtering, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
    extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables the import of all VPN-IPv4 routes into the dummy VRF (`enable-rr-vpn-forwarding`)
2. Advertises extended next-hop encoding capability for VPN-IPv4 routes (`extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4`)

For additional control over next-hop resolution, you may also configure:

```cli
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel
    family vpn
exit
```

This ensures proper next-hop resolution for VPN-IPv4 routes in the dummy VRF context.
