To enforce strict validation of the AS_PATH's terminating AS against the neighbor's configured AS number, use the `enforce-first-as` command in your BGP configuration. Here are the relevant CLI commands:

For global BGP configuration:
```
configure router bgp
    enforce-first-as
exit
```

Alternatively, you can apply it at the group or neighbor level:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    enforce-first-as
exit
```

Or for a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    enforce-first-as
exit
```

This will ensure BGP rejects any routes where the last AS in the AS_PATH doesn't match the configured peer's AS number.
