To enforce strict policy-based tunnel selection using only BGP next-hop routes with a specific administrative tag, configure the following:

```
configure router
    policy-options
        begin
        policy-statement STRICT-TAG-POLICY
            entry 10
                from
                    protocol bgp
                    admin-tag <your-specific-tag-value>
                action accept
            exit
            default-action reject
        commit

    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family ipv4
                        resolution-filter
                            bgp
                            enforce-strict-tunnel-tagging
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
                shortcut-tunnels
                    family ipv4
                        resolution-filter
                            bgp
                            enforce-strict-tunnel-tagging
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
            policy STRICT-TAG-POLICY
        exit
```

Replace `<your-specific-tag-value>` with your actual administrative tag value. This configuration:
1. Creates a policy that only accepts BGP routes with your specified admin tag
2. Enforces strict tunnel tagging for both transport tunnels and shortcut tunnels
3. Applies the policy to BGP next-hop resolution to ensure only tagged paths are considered
