To activate advanced BGP anomaly detection and mitigation features while maintaining existing sessions, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    error-handling
    enforce-first-as
    loop-detect discard-route
exit
```

For specific peer groups or neighbors where you want stricter control over next-hop encoding:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4 vpn-ipv4
    initial-send-delay-zero
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Enable enhanced BGP error handling
2. Enforce AS path validation for EBGP peers
3. Change loop detection to silently discard problematic routes instead of dropping sessions
4. Add strict next-hop encoding verification (when applied to groups/peers)
5. Configure immediate update sending after session establishment

The configuration maintains existing sessions while adding protection against malformed updates and route anomalies.
