To optimize your BGP peering strategy and ensure the "INTERNAL_PEERS" route policy properly filters and modifies outbound advertisements to downstream autonomous systems, apply the following configuration commands on your Nokia routers:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group INTERNAL_PEERS
        type internal
        outbound-route-filtering
        export "INTERNAL_PEERS"
        min-route-advertisement 15
    exit
exit
```

If you need to adjust the purge timer for stale routes:
```cli
configure router bgp
    purge-timer 20
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Designate the peer group as internal
2. Enable outbound route filtering for the group
3. Apply the "INTERNAL_PEERS" export policy to control outbound advertisements
4. Set a more aggressive route advertisement interval (15 seconds)
5. Optionally extend the purge timer for stale routes to 20 minutes
