To configure BGP-labeled unicast for seamless MPLS integration with next-hop address family identifier type 2 (label-ipv4), use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        bgp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
    group <group-name>
        family label-ipv4
        enable-origin-validation label-ipv4
    exit
    neighbor <neighbor-ip>
        family label-ipv4
    exit
exit
```

For enabling add-paths capability (if needed):
```cli
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        label-ipv4 send 16 receive
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` and `<neighbor-ip>` with your specific BGP group name and neighbor IP address. The `send 16` parameter can be adjusted based on your path advertisement requirements.
