Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
Here are the recommended CLI commands to implement BGP graceful restart for IPv6 VPNs while adjusting the hold timer and ensuring session persistence:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 300
        enable-notification
    exit
    group <your-bgp-group-name>
        graceful-restart
            restart-time 300
        exit
        neighbor <peer-ipv6-address>
            graceful-restart
                restart-time 300
            exit
            family vpn-ipv6
                prefix-limit vpn-ipv6 <your-limit-value> idle-timeout 30
            exit
        exit
    exit
    backup-path label-ipv6
exit
```

Key configuration elements:
1. Enabled graceful restart globally and per-neighbor with notification support
2. Set restart-time to 300 seconds (default) for stability
3. Configured prefix limits for VPN-IPv6 with automatic recovery
4. Added BGP fast reroute for labeled IPv6 routes to maintain MPLS services

Adjust the `<your-bgp-group-name>`, `<peer-ipv6-address>`, and `<your-limit-value>` placeholders according to your specific deployment requirements.
