To ensure proper next-hop resolution for BGP-learned IPv6 routes without MPLS labels over your IS-IS shortcut tunnels, configure the following:

```cli
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution
    shortcut-tunnel
        family ipv6
            resolution-filter bgp
            exit
        exit
    exit
    next-hop-res
        use-bgp-routes
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables shortcut tunneling for IPv6 routes under BGP next-hop resolution
2. Adds BGP to the resolution filter for IPv6 routes
3. Enables recursive next-hop resolution using BGP routes (up to 4 levels)

For completeness, also verify that third-party next-hop is disabled unless specifically required for your topology:

```cli
configure router bgp
    no third-party-nexthop
exit
```
