To configure your Nokia router to provide comprehensive visibility of labeled IPv6 and IPv4 VPN routes (SAFI 128) to your BMP monitoring station while maintaining MPLS service integrity, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
# Configure BGP to support required address families
configure router bgp
    family label-ipv4 label-ipv6 vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4 vpn-ipv4
exit

# Enable rapid updates for VPN routes if needed
configure router bgp
    rapid-update label-ipv4 label-ipv6 vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6
exit

# Configure BMP station to monitor all required address families
configure bmp station "BMP_STATION_NAME"
    family ipv4 ipv6 label-ipv4 label-ipv6 vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6
exit
```

Replace `BMP_STATION_NAME` with your actual BMP station name. This configuration:
1. Enables support for both labeled and VPN IPv4/IPv6 address families in BGP
2. Configures extended next-hop encoding capabilities for labeled IPv4 and VPN IPv4 routes
3. Optionally enables rapid updates for these route types
4. Configures the BMP station to monitor all relevant address families
