To enable BGP graceful restart with the F-bit correctly set for L2-VPN, route-target, and flow-specific AFI/SAFIs (IPv4/IPv6) on your Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
    long-lived
        forwarding-bits-set non-fwd
    exit
    group <group-name>
        family l2-vpn route-target flow-ipv4 flow-ipv6
        graceful-restart
        long-lived
            forwarding-bits-set non-fwd
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This configuration:
1. Enables BGP graceful restart globally
2. Sets the F-bit specifically for non-forwarding AFI/SAFIs (L2-VPN, route-target, flow-IPv4, and flow-IPv6)
3. Configures the same settings at the group level
4. Includes the required address families in the BGP group configuration

For neighbor-specific configurations, apply the same settings under `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor` if needed.
