To gracefully preserve BGP sessions during maintenance reboots on your Nokia router, use these CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
    enable-notification
    mp-bgp-keep
    purge-timer 30
exit
```

For specific BGP groups or neighbors where you want to ensure route preservation:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    graceful-restart
    enable-notification
    prefix-limit <family> <high-value> threshold 90 log-only
exit
```

These configurations will:
1. Enable BGP graceful restart helper mode
2. Allow notification-based graceful restarts
3. Retain MP-BGP routes without requiring refreshes 
4. Extend the stale route purge timer to 30 minutes
5. Configure high prefix limits with logging-only enforcement to prevent session drops

The settings help maintain BGP sessions during reboots by keeping routes active longer and allowing neighbors to gracefully handle the restart process.
