Here are the CLI configuration commands to define a BGP peer group "EUROPE-WEST-1" on a Nokia 7750 SR for streamlining route advertisement policies:

```
configure router bgp
    group "EUROPE-WEST-1"
        type external
        peer-as <AS_NUMBER>
        import "EUROPE-WEST-1-INBOUND-POLICY"
        export "EUROPE-WEST-1-OUTBOUND-POLICY"
        graceful-restart
            long-lived
                forwarding-bits-set all
        exit
        neighbor <NEIGHBOR_IP>
            description "European West Edge Router"
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<AS_NUMBER>` with your peer AS number, `<NEIGHBOR_IP>` with the actual neighbor IP addresses, and adjust the policy names ("EUROPE-WEST-1-INBOUND-POLICY"/"OUTBOUND-POLICY") to match your specific route policies.

For dynamic neighbors in the same subnet, you could add:
```
configure router bgp
    group "EUROPE-WEST-1"
        dynamic-neighbor
            prefix <SUBNET_PREFIX> <MASK>
            peer-range <START_IP>-<END_IP>
        exit
        third-party-nexthop
    exit
exit
```
