## User question:
During a multi-regional BGP peering setup on our Nokia 7750 SRs, I need to consolidate several peers from the EU-West-1 region under a common template—what's the proper CLI syntax to define this peer group while ensuring all inherited policies maintain consistency across members?
---
## Proposed answer:
Here's the CLI configuration to create a BGP peer group for EU-West-1 peers with consistent policies:

```
configure router bgp
    group "EU-West-1-Peers"
        type external
        peer-as 12345   # Replace with your actual peer AS number
        import "EU-WEST-INBOUND-POLICY"   # Replace with your import policy name
        export "EU-WEST-OUTBOUND-POLICY"  # Replace with your export policy name
        dynamic-neighbor
            prefix 192.0.2.0/24           # Replace with your EU-West-1 peer subnet
        exit
    exit
exit
```

For static neighbors that should inherit these same policies:
```
configure router bgp
    group "EU-West-1-Peers"
        neighbor 192.0.2.10               # Example specific peer IP
            description "EU-West-1 Peer A"
        exit
        neighbor 192.0.2.20               # Example specific peer IP
            description "EU-West-1 Peer B"
        exit
    exit
exit
