To ensure prefixes from a GR-capable peer remain in a transient state for no longer than 300 seconds before progressing to stable graceful restart mode, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        stale-routes-time 300
    exit
exit
```

If you need to apply this to a specific group or neighbor, use:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    graceful-restart
        stale-routes-time 300
    exit
exit
```

Or for a specific neighbor:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    graceful-restart
        stale-routes-time 300
    exit
exit
```
