To configure the LLGR stale-time parameter to a one-hour duration (3600 seconds), use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    long-lived
        advertised-stale-time 3600
        helper-override-stale-time 3600
    exit
exit
```

Additionally, if you need to adjust the stale routes retention time globally:
```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    stale-routes-time 3600
exit
```

For group or neighbor-specific configurations, use the same parameters under the respective contexts:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> graceful-restart
    long-lived
        advertised-stale-time 3600
        helper-override-stale-time 3600
    exit
    stale-routes-time 3600
exit
```

These commands will ensure proper operation during your maintenance window with a one-hour LLGR stale-time duration.
