To configure a one-hour (3600 seconds) local LLGR stale timer for proper BGP convergence during your maintenance window, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    long-lived
        helper-override-stale-time 3600
        advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors
exit
```

If you need to apply this at a more granular level (per group or neighbor), the structure would be similar but under the respective contexts:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> graceful-restart
    long-lived
        helper-override-stale-time 3600
        advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors
exit
```

For setting the global maximum time to maintain stale routes:
```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    stale-routes-time 3600
exit
```
