To enforce a fixed keepalive interval of 120 seconds and ensure the router rejects neighbor proposals with values below 60 seconds, use the following BGP configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    hold-time 240 min 180
    keepalive 120
exit
```

This configuration:
- Sets the hold-time to 240 seconds (4x the keepAlive interval)
- Enforces a minimum acceptable hold-time of 180 seconds (3x the minimum keepAlive threshold)
- Configures the keepalive timer to 120 seconds

The `min` parameter ensures the router will reject any neighbor proposals attempting to negotiate a hold-time below 180 seconds, which corresponds to rejecting keepalive intervals below 60 seconds (since BGP typically uses a 3:1 ratio between hold-time and keepalive).
------------
