---
## Proposed answer:
To implement the requested BGP session termination after 180 seconds of inactivity while enforcing a minimum acceptable hold time threshold of 60 seconds, use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    hold-time 180 min 60
exit
```

This configuration:
- Sets the BGP hold time to 180 seconds (3 minutes)
- Enforces a minimum acceptable hold time of 60 seconds, rejecting any peer attempts with values below this threshold

Apply this at the global BGP level, or alternatively at specific group/neighbor levels if needed:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    hold-time 180 min 60
exit
```

or 

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    hold-time 180 min 60
exit
