To ensure optimal utilization of all available equal-cost paths for inbound traffic distribution during a core network upgrade involving redundant iBGP speakers on Nokia (Alcatel-Lucent) SR OS devices, configure the following commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    ibgp-multipath
    backup-path ipv4 label-ipv4 ipv6 label-ipv6
    best-path-selection
        ebgp-ibgp-equal ipv4 ipv6 label-ipv4 label-ipv6
        ignore-router-id
    exit
```

These commands enable:
- iBGP multipath load balancing (`ibgp-multipath`)
- Fast reroute capabilities for both labeled and unlabeled IPv4/IPv6 routes (`backup-path`)
- Equal consideration of eBGP and iBGP paths in best-path selection (`ebgp-ibgp-equal`)
- Router ID ignoring for stable path selection (`ignore-router-id`)
