To deprioritize IGP cost evaluation for next-hop reachability when selecting among equivalent BGP paths, configure the following:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ignore-router-id
    exit
```

This configuration modifies the BGP best path selection process to skip the router-ID comparison step (which normally follows IGP metric evaluation in the decision process), effectively reducing the influence of IGP costs when multiple equal BGP paths exist. 

For complete next-hop control in a multi-vendor environment, you may also want to ensure consistent next-hop handling with:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnels
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter
                    sr-policy
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
    group <PEER_GROUP>
        next-hop-self
    exit
```

These commands:
1. Enable SR policy-based next-hop resolution (bypassing IGP)
2. Force next-hop-self advertisement to peers for consistent path evaluation
