To ensure route selection between equivalent NLRIs from legacy BGP peers isn't influenced by next-hop metrics in your multi-vendor migration scenario, configure the following BGP best-path selection parameters:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ignore-nh-metric
        ignore-router-id
    exit
exit
```

For specific neighbor groups where you want to maintain consistent next-hop behavior across vendors:

```
configure router bgp
    group LEGACY_PEERS
        neighbor 192.0.2.1
            third-party-nexthop
        exit
    exit
exit
```

If you're using RSVP LSPs for next-hop resolution and want to ensure consistent metric evaluation:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnels
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter
                    rsvp
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```
