## User question:
"During a multicast VPN IPv6 deployment on our Nokia router infrastructure, we’ve observed that BGP path selection inadvertently prioritizes routes based on router IDs rather than relevant path attributes—how can we adjust the configuration to exclude router IDs from influencing best-path decisions for mvpn-ipv6 routes?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To exclude router IDs from influencing best-path decisions for mvpn-ipv6 routes, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp best-path-selection
    ignore-router-id include-internal mvpn-ipv6
exit
```

This ensures that BGP path selection for mvpn-ipv6 routes will not consider router IDs when determining the best path.
