Here's the CLI configuration to implement stricter ingress filtering for BGP peering with customer 123, combining the existing "cust123-inbound-filter" with additional AS path length constraints:

```
configure router
    policy-options
        begin
        policy-statement aspath-short-enough
            entry 10
                from
                    as-path-length lt 10
                exit
            exit
        commit
    exit
    bgp
        group <customer-group-name>
            neighbor <customer-ip-address>
                import "cust123-inbound-filter AND aspath-short-enough"
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<customer-group-name>` and `<customer-ip-address>` with your actual BGP peer details. This configuration:
1. Creates a new policy "aspath-short-enough" that matches routes with AS paths shorter than 10 hops
2. Combines it with your existing "cust123-inbound-filter" using logical AND operator
3. Applies the combined policy to the specific customer neighbor
