To ensure immediate route advertisement propagation when bringing up new BGP peers and avoid convergence delays, configure the following commands:

```
configure router bgp
    initial-send-delay-zero
    min-route-advertisement 1
    advertise-inactive
exit

# For each BGP group or neighbor where you want fast convergence:
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    initial-send-delay-zero
    min-route-advertisement 1
    advertise-inactive
    graceful-restart
        enable-notification
        long-lived
            advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors
        exit
    exit
exit
```

These settings will:
1. Send updates immediately upon session establishment (`initial-send-delay-zero`)
2. Reduce the minimum advertisement interval to 1 second (`min-route-advertisement 1`)
3. Advertise routes even if they're not the most preferred (`advertise-inactive`)
4. Enable graceful restart capabilities including stale route advertisement (`enable-notification` and `advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors`)
