The router will terminate the TCP session immediately upon hitting the fifth consecutive missed keepalive response (as configured by `keep-count 5`). There are no additional grace periods beyond this threshold—the connection is declared down at that exact point.

Here are the relevant CLI commands to configure these settings:

```cli
configure bmp station "STATION_NAME" connection
    tcp-keepalive
        keep-count 5
        keep-interval 15
    exit
exit
```

If you're configuring BGP keepalives instead, use:
```cli
configure router bgp
    keepalive 30
exit
```

For graceful restart with stale route maintenance:
```cli
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    stale-routes-time 3600
exit
```
