To configure the idle interval threshold to 300 seconds (5 minutes) for initiating keepalive probes on your Nokia routers, use the following BGP configuration command:

```
configure router bgp damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 5 5 60
```

This sets:
- `initial-wait` to 5 minutes (300 seconds)
- `second-wait` to 5 minutes
- `max-wait` to 60 minutes

The configuration should be applied under the appropriate BGP context (global, group, or neighbor level) where you're experiencing the premature session timeouts.
