For optimal BGP session stability with a hold time of 180 seconds, the recommended keepalive interval is **60 seconds** (one-third of the hold time). Here’s the CLI command to configure it:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip> keepalive 60
```

If applying globally to all peers under BGP:
```
configure router bgp keepalive 60
``` 

This maintains the standard 3:1 ratio (keepalive:hold-time) while balancing session stability and CPU efficiency.
