Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To modify the BGP keepalive timer interval to 60 seconds without disrupting existing peerings, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        keepalive 60
        hold-time 180
exit
```

Note: The hold-time should typically be set to 3 times the keepalive value (60 x 3 = 180) for proper BGP operation. Apply these changes under the specific BGP group where you want to modify the timers. The configuration will take effect immediately but won't disrupt existing sessions as BGP peers will negotiate the new timers during the next keepalive exchange.
------------
