To enable BGP link-state address family propagation on your Nokia 7750 routers, use the following configuration sequence:

```cli
configure router bgp
    family bgp-ls
    link-state-import-enable
    group <peer-group-name>
        family bgp-ls
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family bgp-ls
exit all
```

Key points:
1. Enable the `bgp-ls` address family globally under BGP
2. Activate link-state information import with `link-state-import-enable`
3. Configure the same `bgp-ls` family at both group and neighbor levels

For optimal operation, consider adding these optional parameters:
```cli
configure router bgp
    initial-send-delay-zero
    group <peer-group-name>
        prefix-limit bgp-ls <max-routes> threshold 75 idle-timeout 30
exit all
```

This ensures immediate updates upon session establishment and sets reasonable limits for BGP-LS route exchanges.
