To implement a virtual AS (65530) while suppressing both the true local and global autonomous systems in path advertisements on your Nokia router acting as a route reflector, use the following CLI configuration:

```bash
configure router bgp
    local-as 65530 private no-prepend-global-as
    remove-private
exit
```

For legacy peers that require additional compatibility, you may also want to disable 4-byte ASN support and enforce first AS validation where necessary:

```bash
configure router bgp group LEGACY_PEERS
    disable-4byte-asn
    enforce-first-as
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Advertise only the virtual AS (65530) to peers while hiding both the true local and global AS numbers.
2. Remove any remaining private AS numbers from the AS path.
3. Ensure compatibility with legacy peers by enforcing traditional ASN handling.
