To assign a higher local preference of 150 to inbound BGP routes from specific peers, use the following CLI configuration commands:

1. **Configure the BGP group or neighbor with the desired local preference**:
   ```cli
   configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> local-preference 150
   ```
   or for a specific group:
   ```cli
   configure router bgp group <group-name> local-preference 150
   ```

2. **Alternatively, apply a route policy to set the local preference for inbound routes**:
   First, create the policy:
   ```cli
   configure router policy-options begin
   policy-statement SET_LOCAL_PREF
       entry 10
           action accept
           default-action reject
           local-preference 150
       exit
   exit
   commit
   ```

   Then apply it to the peer(s):
   ```cli
   configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> import SET_LOCAL_PREF
   ```

Choose either method based on whether you want to apply the change at the neighbor/group level or via a more flexible policy-based approach.
