To assign a local preference value of 200 to routes received from specific BGP peers on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-IP>
            local-preference 200
```

Alternatively, if you want to apply this to all neighbors in a group:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        local-preference 200
```

For more granular control using route policies:
1. First create the policy:
```
configure router policy-options
    begin
    policy-statement SET_LOCAL_PREF
        entry 10
            action accept
            local-preference 200
    commit
```

2. Then apply it to the desired peers:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-IP>
            import "SET_LOCAL_PREF"
```
