To ensure BGP sessions remain active during your migration without triggering unnecessary route withdrawals, configure Long-Lived Graceful Restart (LLGR) with preserved forwarding state and adjust relevant parameters:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            forwarding-bits-set all
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

For additional stability during control plane transitions:
```
configure router bgp
    advertise-inactive
    loop-detect ignore-loop
    exit
```

These configurations will:
1. Preserve forwarding state across restarts (F-bit=1 for all AFI/SAFI)
2. Continue advertising routes even if they become temporarily inactive
3. Maintain peering while ignoring transient AS path loops

The combination ensures peers retain stale routes during instability while maintaining forwarding continuity.
