To prevent your ASN from appearing in received routes while maintaining the BGP adjacency, configure the following on your Nokia router:

```
configure router bgp
    loop-detect discard-route
exit
```

For more granular control at the group or neighbor level:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    loop-detect discard-route
exit

configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    loop-detect discard-route
exit
```

This configuration will silently discard any routes containing your own ASN in the AS_PATH while keeping the BGP session active. The `discard-route` option is specifically designed for this scenario as it prevents looped routes from entering the RIB without affecting the peering session.
