To enforce BGP loop prevention by terminating sessions when your local AS (AS65530) appears in incoming updates, use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    loop-detect drop-peer
exit
```

This will configure the router to drop the BGP peer session when it detects your own AS number (AS65530) in the AS_PATH of incoming updates. The `drop-peer` action is more strict than the default `ignore-loop` behavior, ensuring proper loop prevention by terminating the session immediately upon detection of a routing loop.

For more granular control, you can apply this at the group or neighbor level if needed:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    loop-detect drop-peer
exit
```

or 

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    loop-detect drop-peer
exit
```
