Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
Here's the optimal BGP/MPLS configuration to enforce asymmetric path control for multicast VPN IPv4:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        vpn-ipv4 send 8 receive none
        mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive none
exit
```

For group-specific configuration (if needed):
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    add-paths
        vpn-ipv4 send 8 receive none
        mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive none
    exit
exit
```

For neighbor-specific configuration (if needed):
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    add-paths
        vpn-ipv4 send 8 receive none
        mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive none
    exit
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Advertise up to 8 distinct paths per IPv4 prefix to downstream peers
2. Prevent acceptance of multipath routes from neighbors
3. Apply to both unicast VPN-IPv4 and multicast VPN-IPv4 routes
