## User question:
"During our MPLS VPN multicast deployment, we need to ensure that our Nokia PE routers can propagate up to eight distinct BGP paths for each mVPNv4 prefix while maintaining compatibility with remote peers capable of multipath route exchange—what’s the optimal way to implement this without disrupting existing unicast routing policies?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure your Nokia PE routers to propagate up to eight distinct BGP paths for each mVPNv4 prefix while maintaining compatibility with remote peers capable of multipath route exchange, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

If you also need to enable this for mVPNv6 prefixes, add:
```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        mvpn-ipv6 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

These configurations will enable both sending and receiving capabilities for up to 8 paths per mVPN prefix without affecting existing unicast routing policies.
