To enable optimal ECMP utilization for your multicast-enabled IPv6 VPN infrastructure, configure the following BGP/MPLS settings on your Nokia PE routers:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        mvpn-ipv6 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

For completeness, if you also need to configure standard VPN-IPv6 routes (non-multicast), use this additional configuration:
```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        vpn-ipv6 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

These configurations will:
1. Allow each PE router to advertise up to 8 distinct paths per mVPNv6 prefix
2. Enable the router to accept multiple received routes for identical prefixes during BGP negotiations
