Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
Here are the CLI configuration commands to enable BGP multipath negotiation for multicast IPv6 VPN routes, allowing propagation of up to eight paths per prefix and accepting multiple received routes:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        mvpn-ipv6 send 8 receive
exit
```

For completeness, if you also need to configure this at the group or neighbor level:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        add-paths
            mvpn-ipv6 send 8 receive
        exit
    exit
    neighbor <ip-address>
        add-paths
            mvpn-ipv6 send 8 receive
        exit
    exit
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Enable sending up to 8 distinct paths per multicast IPv6 VPN prefix
2. Negotiate the capability to receive multiple paths for the same prefixes
