To implement a 15-second dampening interval between successive BGP updates toward all peers, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 0 0.25 0.25 error-interval 0
exit
```

This configuration:
- Sets `initial-wait` to 0 minutes (immediate dampening)
- Configures `second-wait` and `max-wait` to 0.25 minutes (15 seconds)
- Sets `error-interval` to 0 minutes to apply dampening immediately after any error

The values are specified in minutes (0.25 = 15 seconds), and this will apply to all BGP peers under the global BGP configuration.
