## Proposed answer:
To adjust BGP monitoring thresholds on your Nokia router, use the following CLI sequence to access the relevant configuration submenu:

```
configure router bgp
monitor
```

From this context, you can configure various BGP monitoring parameters. For example, to set prefix limits with thresholds (which includes monitoring capabilities), navigate to either the group or neighbor level:

For group-level configuration:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
prefix-limit <family> <limit> threshold <percentage>
```

For neighbor-specific configuration:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
prefix-limit <family> <limit> threshold <percentage>
```

Replace `<group-name>`, `<family>`, `<limit>`, `<percentage>`, and `<ip-address>` with your specific values.
