To adjust BGP monitoring thresholds on your Nokia router, follow this CLI sequence:

```
configure router
    bgp
        monitor
```

This will take you into the BGP monitor configuration sub-mode where you can modify monitoring parameters. From here, you can configure specific thresholds and actions based on your requirements. For example, to set a prefix limit with a threshold:

```
prefix-limit ipv4 50000 threshold 75 idle-timeout 30
```

Or to enable logging without shutting down the session:

```
prefix-limit ipv4 50000 threshold 75 log-only
```
