To modify BGP-based VPN routing policies on a Nokia NSP platform without triggering route-refresh requests and ensuring MP-BGP prefixes remain stable in the RIB-IN table, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    mp-bgp-keep
    purge-timer 0
exit
```

The `mp-bgp-keep` command prevents route-refresh messages from being issued during VPN route policy changes, while `purge-timer 0` ensures stale routes are never purged from RIB-IN. This combination maintains route stability throughout the reconfiguration.
