To ensure MP-BGP prefixes persist in RIB-IN during route policy modifications without relying on periodic route refresh negotiations, enable the `mp-bgp-keep` command under the BGP configuration context. Here’s the CLI command:

```
configure router bgp
    mp-bgp-keep
exit
```

This prevents route refresh messages from being issued when VPN route policies change, retaining all MP-BGP routes in RIB-IN. Optionally, you can also adjust the `purge-timer` to a higher value (e.g., 30 minutes) as a secondary measure:

```
configure router bgp
    purge-timer 30
exit
```
