## User question:
"During a recent network upgrade involving multiple AS hops, we observed inconsistent BGP session stability when EBGP updates traverse three intermediary nodes; what’s the recommended method to adjust the time-to-live parameter on a Nokia router to ensure reliable propagation without exceeding the typical hop-count constraints?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To adjust the TTL parameter for EBGP sessions traversing multiple hops on a Nokia router, use the `multihop` command under the BGP neighbor configuration. For three intermediary nodes (total of 4 hops including the endpoints), set the TTL to at least 5 to ensure reliable propagation while staying within typical hop-count constraints:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            multihop 5
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This ensures the BGP packets have sufficient TTL to traverse all intermediate hops without being discarded.
