Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure your Nokia router to support up to eight distinct BGP paths for IPv4 prefixes in a multicast VPN service while maintaining multipath compatibility with peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        vpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
        mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
exit
```

If you're applying this to specific BGP groups or neighbors, the configuration would look like this:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    add-paths
        vpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
        mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
    exit
exit

configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    add-paths
        vpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
        mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

These commands enable both sending and receiving capabilities for up to 8 paths per prefix for both VPN-IPv4 and multicast VPN IPv4 routes.
