To enable the advertisement of up to eight distinct BGP paths per IPv4 prefix and support multipath negotiation for inbound route acceptance in your multicast VPN service, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
        exit
    backup-path ipv4
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables BGP Add-Paths for MVPN IPv4 with a send limit of 8 paths per prefix
2. Negotiates to receive multiple paths for each prefix
3. Enables BGP fast reroute for IPv4 routes to utilize backup paths when available

The configuration can be applied at either the global BGP level, group level, or neighbor level depending on your specific topology requirements.
