Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
Here's the optimal configuration to advertise up to three BGP paths for each MVPN IPv6 prefix while suppressing multipath reception:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        mvpn-ipv6 send 3 receive none
    exit
```

If you also want to ensure consistent path selection across EBGP peers regardless of router IDs:
```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ignore-router-id include-internal mvpn-ipv6
    exit
```

These commands will:
1. Enable advertising up to 3 paths per MVPN IPv6 prefix
2. Disable receiving multiple paths (suppressing multipath reception)
3. Optionally make path selection independent of router IDs for more stable routing
