Here are the CLI configuration commands to establish an eBGP session with your new transit provider:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group "TRANSIT_PROVIDER"
            type external
            peer-as <provider_as_number>
            neighbor 192.168.10.1
                description "Transit Provider eBGP Session"
                multihop 64
                enforce-first-as
                prefix-limit ipv4 <max_routes> threshold 75 idle-timeout 15
                authentication-key <your_secure_password> hash
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace these placeholders with your actual values:
- `<provider_as_number>` - Your transit provider's AS number
- `<max_routes>` - Maximum number of IPv4 prefixes you'll accept (e.g., 500000)
- `<your_secure_password>` - Your MD5 authentication key

For additional security, consider adding:
```
            neighbor 192.168.10.1
                ttl-security minimum 254
                exit
```

