---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure each BGP update sourced from a local interface retains its own interface IP as the next-hop attribute, use the `next-hop-self` command in the BGP group or neighbor configuration. Here are the CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        next-hop-self
exit
```

Or for a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            next-hop-self
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This will force the router to use its local interface IP as the next-hop for all advertised routes, regardless of their origin.
