To maintain the original next-hop attribute when redistributing BGP-labeled IPv4 routes to a designated peer group during your multi-vendor migration, use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        next-hop-unchanged label-ipv4
        no next-hop-self
        exit
    exit
```

For EBGP peers in the same subnet, also enable:
```
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        third-party-nexthop
        exit
    exit
```

If you need to advertise extended next-hop capabilities to peers:
```
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
        exit
    exit
```

These configurations will preserve the original next-hop attributes while ensuring proper handling of labeled IPv4 routes across your mixed vendor environment.
