To minimize unnecessary BGP route advertisements while maintaining optimal path selection during your core network upgrade, consider these advanced configuration adjustments:

```cli
# Configure prefix limits to prevent excessive route advertisements
configure router bgp group CORE_UPGRADE
    prefix-limit ipv4 500000 threshold 75 idle-timeout 15
    prefix-limit ipv6 200000 threshold 75 idle-timeout 15
exit

# Increase route advertisement intervals to reduce churn
configure router bgp group CORE_UPGRADE
    min-route-advertisement 60
exit

# Enable multipath with restrictions for better load balancing
configure router bgp
    multipath 8 ebgp 4 ibgp 4 restrict same-neighbor-as
exit

# Optimize best path selection stability
configure router bgp best-path-selection
    ignore-router-id
exit
```

Key features implemented:
- Prefix limits with warnings at 75% capacity and automatic recovery
- Extended advertisement interval (60 seconds)
- Conservative multipath settings with neighbor AS restriction
- Router ID ignoring for more stable path selection

These settings will help maintain network stability while reducing unnecessary route propagation during the upgrade process.
