To deprioritize BGP routes with failed RPKI origin validation while keeping them in the routing table, configure the following on your Nokia SR OS platform:

1. Enable origin validation for the desired address families:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    enable-origin-validation ipv4 ipv6
exit
```

2. Configure BGP best path selection to consider origin validation states without marking invalid routes as unusable:
```
configure router bgp best-path-selection
    compare-origin-validation-state
    no origin-invalid-unusable
exit
```

This configuration will:
- Mark routes with their RPKI validation state (Valid/NotFound/Invalid)
- Prefer routes with better validation states during path selection (Valid > NotFound > Invalid)
- Keep invalid routes in the routing table but deprioritize them
