To modify the BGP best-path selection algorithm to deprioritize prefixes failing RPKI-based origin validation, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        origin-invalid-unusable
    exit
    group <group-name>
        enable-origin-validation ipv4 ipv6
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your specific BGP group name. This configuration will:
1. Mark routes with invalid RPKI validation as unusable (preventing them from being selected as best path)
2. Enable origin validation for both IPv4 and IPv6 routes on the specified BGP group

The `origin-invalid-unusable` command ensures that invalid routes are neither propagated to downstream neighbors nor installed in the forwarding table.
------------
