To implement efficient route filter list propagation between BGP peers on your Nokia router, use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    outbound-route-filtering
    exit
    group <peer-group-name>
        outbound-route-filtering
        dynamic-neighbor
        initial-send-delay-zero
        enable-peer-tracking
    exit
```

For VPN-IP routes, you may also want to adjust the purge timer:
```
configure router bgp
    purge-timer 15
exit
```

Replace `<peer-group-name>` with your actual BGP peer group name. This configuration enables outbound route filtering at both global and group levels, allows dynamic neighbor sessions, ensures immediate route updates upon session establishment, and accelerates convergence with peer tracking.
