To enable Outbound Route Filtering (ORF) capability negotiation in your BGP session configuration, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            outbound-route-filtering
                extended-community
                    send-orf
                    accept-orf
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This configuration enables both send and receive ORF capabilities for dynamic inbound route filtering adjustments.

For more granular control, you can optionally specify community IDs in the `send-orf` command:
```
send-orf target:65000:100
``` 

Where `target:65000:100` would be replaced with your specific route target extended community.
