To disable entropy-based load balancing specifically for BGP-stitched tunnels while preserving ECMP behavior for regular IP routes, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    no override-tunnel-elc
exit
```

This command disables the entropy label capability (ELC) on BGP tunnels, which addresses your requirement for BGP-stitched VXLAN EVPN overlays without affecting standard ECMP behavior for IP routes.
