To configure a Nokia router's BGP peering to passively listen for established sessions without actively initiating outbound connection attempts, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        passive
exit
```

Or for a specific neighbor within a group:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            passive
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables passive mode, allowing the router to accept incoming BGP connections but not initiate them.
