To configure a BGP peer group on a Nokia device that only accepts inbound sessions without actively establishing outbound TCP connections, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        passive
        dynamic-neighbor
            dynamic-neighbor-limit <max-peers>
        exit
exit
```

Replace `<peer-group-name>` with your desired group name and `<max-peers>` with the maximum number of dynamic peers you want to allow. The `passive` command ensures the router only listens for incoming BGP connections without initiating outbound sessions. The `dynamic-neighbor` context with `dynamic-neighbor-limit` allows dynamic peering within the specified limit.
