To address the intermittent BGP session drops due to TCP fragmentation, enable Path MTU Discovery for your BGP sessions. Here are the recommended CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    path-mtu-discovery
exit

# Optionally, apply at the group or neighbor level if needed:
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    path-mtu-discovery
exit
```

For additional stability, consider enabling peer tracking and adjusting loop detection settings:

```
configure router bgp
    enable-peer-tracking
    loop-detect drop-peer
exit
```

These configurations will dynamically adjust the MTU for BGP sessions while improving overall session stability.
