To configure an eBGP session with a remote peer ASN of 65001 on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        type external
        peer-as 65001
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your desired BGP group name. This sets up the basic eBGP peering with the specified remote ASN. 

For additional parameters like multihop or enforce-first-as, you would add those under the group or neighbor context as needed. For example, if the peer is multiple hops away:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        type external
        peer-as 65001
        multihop <ttl-value>
exit
```
