To automatically terminate the BGP session when inbound routes are rejected by the 'core-routes' import policy, use the `prefix-limit` command with the `post-import` option. This ensures the limit is enforced only after applying import policies. Configure it under the specific BGP neighbor or group:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    prefix-limit ipv4 0 idle-timeout forever post-import
exit
```

Or for a specific group:
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    prefix-limit ipv4 0 idle-timeout forever post-import
exit
```

This configuration sets the prefix limit to zero with `post-import`, causing the session to terminate immediately if no routes pass the import policy. The `idle-timeout forever` ensures the session stays down until manually reset.
