To restrict BGP next-hop resolution strictly to the 'core-routes' IP route policy within the Route Table Manager, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution
    shortcut-tunnels
        family ipv4
            resolution-filter
                no sr-policy
                no labeled-routes
                route-table-mgr core-routes
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Disables SR policy resolution (`no sr-policy`)
2. Disables labeled route resolution (`no labeled-routes`) 
3. Explicitly specifies the 'core-routes' route policy for next-hop resolution

The configuration ensures BGP next-hop resolution will only consider routes present in the specified 'core-routes' policy.
