To configure a local preference value of 200 for incoming BGP updates on your Nokia 7750 SR platform, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    local-preference 200
exit
```

If you need to apply this setting at a more granular level (e.g., for a specific BGP group or neighbor), you can use these variations:

For a BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    local-preference 200
exit
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    local-preference 200
exit
```

These configurations will ensure BGP-learned routes have a higher local preference (200) than your static routes (default preference 5), making them preferred in the route selection process.
