Here are the recommended CLI configurations to implement graceful handling of up to 5,000 IPv6 BGP routes with an 80% utilization alert while maintaining session stability:

```bash
# Configure BGP group or neighbor for IPv6 prefix limits
configure router bgp 
    group <ISP_GROUP_NAME>
        family ipv6
        prefix-limit ipv6 5000 threshold 80 log-only
exit

# Enable BGP backup paths for IPv6 stability
configure router bgp
    backup-path ipv6
exit

# Optional: Configure extended next-hop encoding if needed
configure router bgp
    group <ISP_GROUP_NAME>
        extended-nh-encoding
exit
```

Key features implemented:
- Sets a 5,000 route limit for IPv6 prefixes
- Triggers alerts at 80% utilization (4,000 routes)
- Uses `log-only` to maintain session stability if limit is exceeded
- Enables fast reroute capabilities for IPv6 traffic
- Includes optional extended next-hop encoding support
