To authorize dynamic BGP neighbor relationships from the 192.168.100.0/24 management subnet while maintaining existing security policies, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        type internal
        dynamic-neighbor
            prefix 192.168.100.0/24
        exit
        peer-as <YOUR_LOCAL_AS>
    exit
    dynamic-neighbor-limit <MAX_DYNAMIC_SESSIONS>
exit
```

Replace `<YOUR_LOCAL_AS>` with your autonomous system number and `<MAX_DYNAMIC_SESSIONS>` with an appropriate limit for dynamic BGP sessions. This configuration:
1. Creates a dedicated BGP group for dynamic peers
2. Authorizes connections from the 192.168.100.0/24 subnet
3. Maintains control through session limits
4. Preserves existing static neighbor configurations

For additional security, consider applying route policies to this group to maintain your existing security posture.
