To configure your Nokia router for dynamic BGP peering with devices in the 192.168.10.0/24 testbed network, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        type external
        peer-as <REMOTE_AS_NUMBER>
        dynamic-neighbor
            prefix 192.168.10.0/24
        exit
        extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4 vpn-ipv4
    exit
    next-hop-resolution
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<REMOTE_AS_NUMBER>` with the autonomous system number of your testbed network devices. This configuration:
- Creates a BGP group for dynamic peers
- Specifies the prefix range for accepting dynamic BGP sessions
- Enables extended next-hop encoding capabilities
- Configures basic next-hop resolution

For authentication, add MD5 authentication under the group or neighbor configuration if required:

```
configure router bgp
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        authentication-key "<PASSWORD>" hash
    exit
exit
```
