To configure 192.0.2.1 as the primary IPv4 loopback address for optimizing BGP route reflector performance on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```bash
configure router bgp
    router-id 192.0.2.1
    optimal-route-reflection
        location 1 primary-ip-address 192.0.2.1
    exit
exit
```

If you also want to enable BGP fast reroute for IPv4 routes, add:

```bash
configure router bgp
    backup-path ipv4
exit
```
