To configure BGP optimal route reflection with the designated primary IPv6 address 2001:db8::1 while maintaining path diversity, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    orr location "RR_LOCATION"
        primary-ipv6-address 2001:db8::1
        secondary-ipv6-address <secondary_ipv6_address>
        tertiary-ipv6-address <tertiary_ipv6_address>
    exit
    backup-path ipv6
exit
```

Replace `<secondary_ipv6_address>` and `<tertiary_ipv6_address>` with your specific secondary and tertiary IPv6 addresses to maintain path diversity. The `backup-path ipv6` command ensures fast reroute capability for IPv6 routes.
