Here are the CLI configuration commands to designate 2001:db8::1 as the primary IPv6 RID for optimal route reflection and configure next-hop-self for legacy peers:

```
configure router bgp
    orr
        location
            primary-ipv6-address 2001:db8::1
        exit
    exit
    group <legacy-peer-group-name>
        next-hop-self
    exit
```

For additional redundancy, you could optionally add secondary and tertiary IPv6 addresses under the same location context. The `next-hop-self` configuration ensures proper routing for legacy peers that don't support IPv6 route reflection natively.
