To ensure instant propagation of route withdrawals during BGP peer decommissioning without hold-down periods affecting convergence, configure the following commands:

```
configure router bgp
    rapid-withdrawal
    enable-peer-tracking
    no purge-timer
exit
```

These settings will:
1. Disable the delay on sending BGP withdrawals (`rapid-withdrawal`)
2. Enable immediate peer drop detection when routes are removed (`enable-peer-tracking`)
3. Remove the default 10-minute purge timer for stale routes (`no purge-timer`)

For the specific neighbor being decommissioned, you should also clear their session to trigger immediate withdrawal propagation:
```
clear router bgp neighbor <ip-address>
```
