To ensure instantaneous propagation of route withdrawals when decommissioning a legacy BGP peer, configure the following commands:

```
configure router bgp
    rapid-withdrawal
    no purge-timer
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Disable the delay on sending BGP withdrawals (`rapid-withdrawal`)
2. Remove the default 10-minute purge timer for stale routes (`no purge-timer`)

For immediate effect, you should also administratively shut down the BGP peer:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <peer-address>
    shutdown
exit
```
