To ensure internally generated prefixes from your Nokia routers are properly exported to the BMP collector, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure
    bmp
        station "BMP_STATION_NAME"
            connection
                local-address <local-ip-address>
                router <router-instance>
            exit
            report-local-routes
        exit
    exit
    router bgp
        monitor
            route-monitoring pre-policy post-policy
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `BMP_STATION_NAME` with your BMP station identifier, `<local-ip-address>` with the router's source IP for BMP communication, and `<router-instance>` with the appropriate routing instance (e.g., `Base`). The `route-monitoring` command ensures both pre-policy and post-policy routes are sent to the collector.
