To ensure locally generated prefixes are properly exported to your BMP collector while maintaining existing routing policies, use these CLI configuration commands:

```
configure
    bmp
        station "BMP_COLLECTOR_NAME"
            connection
                router "Base"  # Or specify your VPRN instance if applicable
            exit
            route-monitoring pre-policy post-policy
        exit
    exit
```

For comprehensive monitoring, you may also want to add these optional configurations:
```
configure
    router bgp
        monitor
            route-monitoring pre-policy post-policy
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration will:
1. Establish the BMP connection to your collector
2. Enable both pre-policy and post-policy route monitoring
3. Maintain all existing routing policies while ensuring local prefixes are visible to the BMP collector

The `pre-policy` option ensures you see raw incoming routes, while `post-policy` shows the routes after policy application. Both are recommended for complete visibility.
