To restrict your Nokia router's resolution of unlabeled BGP prefixes exclusively through BGP next-hops and SR-ISIS tunnels while excluding other LSP types, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunn family ipv4 resolution-filter bgp sr-isis
```

If you also need to enforce strict tunnel tagging to ensure only specifically tagged LSPs are considered, add this command:
```cli
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunn family ipv4 enforce-strict-tunnel-tagging
```

For labeled routes (if applicable), apply the same restrictions under the `labeled-routes` context:
```cli
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family ipv4 resolution-filter bgp sr-isis
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family ipv4 enforce-strict-tunnel-tagging
```
