To ensure BGP-labeled routes on your Nokia routers only resolve their next-hops through specific SR-TE tunnels, configure the following:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel family ipv4
                resolution-filter sr-te
                enforce-strict-tunnel-tagging
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Restricts next-hop resolution exclusively to SR-TE tunnels (`resolution-filter sr-te`)
2. Enforces strict tunnel tagging to ensure only explicitly tagged SR-TE tunnels are considered (`enforce-strict-tunnel-tagging`)

Make sure your SR-TE tunnels are properly configured with admin tags if you're using the strict tagging enforcement.
