1. Restricts next-hop resolution for BGP-labeled routes to only RSVP-TE (`rsvp`) and SR-TE (`sr-te`) tunnel types under the `ipv4` family.
2. Enables strict tunnel tagging to ensure only explicitly tagged LSPs are considered for resolution.

For peer-specific enforcement, apply this configuration within the appropriate BGP group or neighbor context where the selective binding is required.
