## User question:
"During a maintenance window where we're implementing BGP graceful restart across our Nokia router fleet to minimize traffic disruption, what’s the proper CLI syntax to ensure the routers signal a maximum recovery interval of 600 seconds to neighboring peers?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure your Nokia router to signal a maximum recovery interval of 600 seconds (restart-time) to BGP neighbors during graceful restart, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 600
    exit
exit
```

If you need to apply this to specific BGP groups or neighbors instead of globally, use these variations:

For a specific group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 600
    exit
exit
```

For a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 600
    exit
exit
---
