To ensure proper next-hop resolution for labeled IPv4 BGP routes when dynamically programming tunnels via gRPC, configure the following under BGP next-hop resolution:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family ipv4
                        resolution-filter
                            rib-api
                            bgp
                            sr-policy
                            rsvp
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration enables the router to use gRPC-programmed tunnels (via `rib-api`), BGP label-unicast tunnels (`bgp`), segment routing policies (`sr-policy`), and RSVP tunnels (`rsvp`) for next-hop resolution of labeled IPv4 BGP routes. The order of priority is determined by the sequence of the commands under `resolution-filter`.
