To configure your Nokia router to dynamically advertise only active IPv4 prefixes from the routing table via BGP using the 'core-routes' policy statement, follow these steps:

1. First, create the policy statement to match active routes:
```
configure router policy-options
begin
policy-statement "core-routes"
    entry 10
        from protocol direct
        from protocol static
        from protocol ospf
        accept
    exit
commit
```

2. Apply the policy as an export filter in BGP:
```
configure router bgp
    export "core-routes"
exit
```

3. Verify the policy is applied correctly:
```
show router policy "core-routes"
show router bgp neighbor <peer-ip> advertised-routes
```

This configuration will ensure only active routes (direct, static, and OSPF) from the routing table are advertised via BGP. Adjust the protocols in the policy statement as needed to match your specific routing environment.
