To configure your Nokia router to advertise all active IPv4 routes from the routing table via BGP using the existing 'core-routes' policy, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        rib-management
            ipv4
                route-table-import "core-routes"
            exit
        exit
        group "your-group-name"
            neighbor "peer-ip-address"
                export "core-routes"
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `"your-group-name"` with your BGP group name and `"peer-ip-address"` with the actual downstream peer IP address. This configuration:
1. Imports active IPv4 routes from the routing table into BGP using the 'core-routes' policy
2. Exports these routes to the specified BGP peer using the same policy

For additional capabilities if needed (like labeled IPv4 or VPN IPv4), you can add under the group or neighbor context:
```
extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4 vpn-ipv4
```
