To properly resolve next-hop addresses for labeled IPv4 routes during a core network migration while maintaining the Nokia PE routers' role as non-participants in LDP or RSVP-TE signaling, apply the following configuration:

```cli
# Enable extended next-hop encoding for labeled IPv4 routes
configure router bgp
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
exit

# Configure next-hop resolution for labeled IPv4 routes without enabling LDP/RSVP
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes
    transport-tunnel
        family label-ipv4
            resolution-filter
                # Explicitly disable RSVP/LDP if needed (though absence implies non-participation)
                no rsvp
                no ldp
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit

# Optionally preserve third-party next-hop behavior if required for eBGP scenarios
configure router bgp
    third-party-nexthop
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Advertises BGP capability to handle labeled IPv4 routes with extended next-hop encoding
2. Configures next-hop resolution for labeled IPv4 routes while ensuring the router won't participate in RSVP/LDP signaling
3. Maintains optional third-party next-hop behavior for eBGP peers in the same subnet
