To configure the secondary IPv6 address 2001:db8::2 as a loopback interface for optimal BGP route reflection on your Nokia 7750 SR, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    optimal-route-reflection
        location 1
            secondary-ipv6-address 2001:db8::2
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Additionally, enable BGP fast reroute for IPv6 to ensure rapid failover:

```
configure router bgp
    backup-path ipv6
exit
``` 

These commands will assign the secondary IPv6 address to the route reflector location and enable backup path functionality for IPv6 routes.
