Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To ensure your Nokia router propagates the link-bandwidth attribute to external BGP peers for IPv4 route advertisements while maintaining compatibility with third-party devices, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
            exit
        neighbor <peer-ip>
            link-bandwidth
                send-to-ebgp ipv4
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

If you also need to handle third-party next-hop scenarios for better compatibility:
```cli
configure router bgp
    third-party-nexthop
    exit
```

For cases where you want to accept or automatically add link-bandwidth attributes from EBGP peers:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` and `<peer-ip>` with your actual BGP group name and peer IP address respectively.
