To configure your Nokia router to propagate the link-bandwidth attribute as an extended community for IPv4 routes toward external BGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

For scenarios where you need to maintain third-party next-hop behavior with EBGP peers in the same subnet, also include:

```
configure router bgp
