Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To ensure BGP-learned prefixes without explicit labels are properly propagated across your MPLS-over-GRE tunnels, configure the following:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            shortcut-tunn ipv4
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter gre
                    resolution any
            exit
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel ipv4
                    family ipv4
                        resolution-filter gre
                        resolution any
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

If you also want to include SR policies for next-hop resolution, add this under the `resolution-filter` sections:
```
resolution-filter gre sr-policy
```

For more granular control over which routes are eligible for resolution, create a route policy and apply it:
```
configure router
    policy-options
        begin
        policy-statement BGP-NH-POLICY
            entry 10
                from
                    protocol bgp
                exit
                action accept
                exit
            exit
        commit
    exit
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            policy "BGP-NH-POLICY"
        exit
    exit
```
