The underlying mechanism for next-hop resolution of unlabeled BGP prefixes involves configuring specific tunnel types in the next-hop resolution context. Here are the relevant CLI commands to properly resolve next-hops for unlabeled BGP prefixes:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnel
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter
                    sr-policy
                    ldp
                    rsvp
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

For VPN-IP routes, ensure proper forwarding with:
```
configure router bgp
    enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        sr-policy
                        ldp
                        rsvp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

These configurations allow the router to resolve next-hops using Segment Routing policies, LDP, or RSVP tunnels for both unlabeled IPv4 BGP routes and VPN-IP routes.
