To administratively disable a specific BGP peer while preserving its session parameters, use the `shutdown` command under the neighbor configuration. This will gracefully bring down the adjacency without removing the configured settings:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> shutdown
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP group and `<ip-address>` with the peer's IP address. To reactivate the peer later, simply remove the shutdown command:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> no shutdown
```

This method maintains all existing configurations for the peer while temporarily disabling the session.
