To ensure proper BGP next-hop resolution over IS-IS SR tunnels during a multi-vendor core migration while maintaining existing MPLS services, configure the following on your Nokia 7750:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            shortcut-tunn family ipv4
                resolution-filter sr-isis rsvp
            exit
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel family ipv4
                    resolution-filter sr-isis rsvp
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Key considerations:
1. Include both `sr-isis` and `rsvp` in the resolution filter to allow BGP to use either IS-IS SR tunnels or existing RSVP-TE LSPs for next-hop resolution.
2. This maintains backward compatibility with existing MPLS services while enabling traffic steering over the new IS-IS SR tunnels.
3. The configuration applies to both unlabeled routes (under `shortcut-tunn`) and labeled routes (under `labeled-routes`).

The router will prefer IS-IS SR tunnels when available (due to lower protocol preference), but will fall back to RSVP-TE LSPs if needed, ensuring continuous service during migration.
------------
