To ensure proper path selection aligns with your intended traffic engineering policies during the transition to SR-based transport, you need to configure the BGP next-hop resolution to prioritize specific OSPF instances. Here are the relevant CLI commands:

For IPv4:
```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunn family ipv4 resolution-filter
    no sr-ospf
exit
```

For IPv6:
```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunn family ipv6 resolution-filter
    no sr-ospf3
exit
```

These commands disable the default behavior where BGP automatically uses the lowest-preference OSPF instance for next-hop resolution. After applying these changes, you'll need to explicitly configure your preferred path selection method (such as `sr-te` or `sr-policy`) based on your traffic engineering requirements.
