To ensure OSPF-originated segment-routed tunnels take precedence over other protocol-derived paths for BGP next-hop resolution, configure the following:

For IPv4:
```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunn family ipv4 resolution-filter sr-ospf
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family ipv4 resolution-filter sr-ospf
```

For IPv6:
```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunn family ipv6 resolution-filter sr-ospf3
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family ipv6 resolution-filter sr-ospf3
```

These commands prioritize OSPF-originated SR tunnels in the BGP next-hop resolution process, ensuring they are selected over ECMP paths from other protocols.
