## Proposed answer:
To configure your Nokia routers to propagate locally defined SR policies via BGP to peers capable of handling the SR Policy IPv4 AFI, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    sr-policy-import
    group <group-name>
        family sr-policy-ipv4
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family sr-policy-ipv4
            graceful-restart
                long-lived
                    forwarding-bits-set all
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Ensure the BGP peers are configured to support the `sr-policy-ipv4` address family. This setup will import local SR policies into BGP and advertise them to the specified peers while maintaining forwarding state during restarts.
