To configure your Nokia routers to propagate locally defined SRv6 policies via BGP while maintaining traffic engineering constraints, use the following CLI sequence:

```
configure router bgp
    sr-policy-import
    exit
configure router bgp group <group_name>
    family sr-policy-ipv4
    neighbor <neighbor_ip>
        family sr-policy-ipv4
        extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
        advertise-ipv6-next-hops label-ipv4
        next-hop-self
        exit
    exit
```

For each SRv6 policy you want to advertise, ensure it has a color attribute matching any color extended communities in your BGP routes. This configuration:
1. Imports SR policies into BGP
2. Enables SR-Policy IPv4 address family
3. Configures extended next-hop encoding capabilities
4. Advertises IPv6 next-hops for labeled IPv4 routes
5. Forces next-hop-self behavior

The policies will be propagated to neighbors supporting the SR-Policy IPv4 address family while respecting their color-based traffic engineering constraints.
