To ensure deterministic path selection while maintaining community-based policy alignment for labeled IPv4 routes in your segment-routing-enabled MPLS core, implement the following configuration on your Nokia router:

```cli
# Enable extended next-hop encoding for labeled IPv4 routes
configure router bgp 
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
exit

# Configure BGP next-hop resolution to use SR policies and enforce community-based path selection
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution
    # Apply a policy to control eligible resolving routes (replace <policy-name> with your actual policy)
    policy "<policy-name>"
    
    # Configure labeled routes context
    labeled-routes
        transport-tunnel family ipv4
            resolution-filter
                # Prioritize SR policies for next-hop resolution
                sr-policy
                # Fall back to RSVP if needed (optional)
                rsvp
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables proper advertisement/reception of labeled IPv4 routes via BGP
2. Uses the highest-numbered color community to select the appropriate SR policy
3. Provides deterministic path selection by:
   - First attempting resolution via SR policies matching the route's color community
   - Optionally falling back to RSVP tunnels if needed
4. Maintains policy alignment through the applied route policy
