## User question:
"During a planned maintenance window where we're performing a controlled restart on our Nokia router fleet, what’s the recommended approach to ensure BGP neighbor adjacencies maintain stale routes for the full 900-second grace period without prematurely flushing them from the RIB?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure BGP neighbor adjacencies maintain stale routes for the full 900-second grace period during a controlled restart, configure the following commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        stale-routes-time 900
        long-lived
            advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Additionally, adjust the purge timer to match or exceed the grace period:
```
configure router bgp
    purge-timer 15
exit
```

These settings will keep stale routes in the RIB for 900 seconds (15 minutes) and allow them to be advertised to all neighbors during the maintenance window.
