If the stale route timer is set to 300 seconds (5 minutes), the maximum duration these routes could persist in the RIB before being purged depends on the `purge-timer` setting. By default, the `purge-timer` is set to 10 minutes. Therefore, with a stale route timer of 300 seconds, the routes would persist for a maximum of 300 seconds (5 minutes) before being purged if the neighboring peer fails to re-establish the session.

To configure these settings:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        stale-routes-time 300
    exit
    purge-timer 10
exit
