To optimize TCP persistent connections on your Nokia 7750 SR router and mitigate intermittent session drops under high-throughput conditions, apply the following TCP keepalive tuning:

```
configure bmp station "BMP_STATION_NAME" connection
    tcp-keepalive
        idle 300
        interval 30
        retries 3
    exit
exit
```

For BGP-related TCP session stability, consider these additional optimizations:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        stale-routes-time 600
    exit
    group "PEER_GROUP_NAME"
        tcp-mss 1460
        tcp-authentication-key "SECURE_KEY"
    exit
exit
```

These adjustments:
1. Set proactive TCP keepalives to detect stale connections faster
2. Extend stale route retention during restarts
3. Optimize MSS size for better throughput
4. Add TCP authentication for session integrity

Adjust the values based on your specific traffic patterns and failure tolerance thresholds. For critical applications, also ensure sufficient buffer allocations and QoS prioritization.
