To prioritize the IPv6 address `2001:db8::3/128` as the preferred route reflector source, configure the following commands:

```cli
configure router bgp orr location
    primary-ipv6-address 2001:db8::3/128
exit
```

Additionally, enable BGP fast reroute for IPv6 to ensure optimal path selection during failures:

```cli
configure router bgp
    backup-path ipv6
exit
``` 

These commands will set `2001:db8::3/128` as the primary IPv6 address for BGP optimal route reflection and activate backup path functionality for IPv6 routes.
