To maintain the original BGP next-hop attribute during route advertisements between EBGP peers in the same /24 transit segment, use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    third-party-nexthop
exit

configure router bgp group <group_name>
    next-hop-unchanged
    no next-hop-self
exit
```

For specific neighbors, you can apply the configuration at the neighbor level instead:

```
configure router bgp group <group_name> neighbor <ip_address>
    next-hop-unchanged
    no next-hop-self
exit
```

This ensures that:
1. `third-party-nexthop` preserves the original next-hop for EBGP peers in the same subnet
2. `next-hop-unchanged` prevents next-hop modification when advertising routes to peers in the group
3. `no next-hop-self` explicitly disables any next-hop self behavior
------------
