To ensure BGP route advertisements maintain the original next-hop attribute during EBGP sessions between Nokia and Cisco devices in the same /24 transit segment, use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    third-party-nexthop
exit
```

Alternatively, if you want to apply this setting at the group or neighbor level for more granular control:

```
configure router bgp group <group_name>
    next-hop-unchanged
exit
```

Or for a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group_name> neighbor <ip_address>
    next-hop-unchanged
exit
```

These commands will prevent the router from rewriting the next-hop to the local interface address when advertising routes to EBGP peers in the same subnet.
