To implement tunnel-based next-hop resolution for BGP-labeled VPNv4 routes while maintaining VPRN service integrity, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family vpn
                        resolution-filter
                            sr-ospf3
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
            shortcut-tunn
                family vpn
                    resolution-filter
                        sr-ospf3
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
        enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables transport tunnel resolution for VPN-IP routes (both IPv4/IPv6)
2. Uses SR-OSPF3 tunnels for next-hop resolution in both primary and shortcut tunnel paths
3. Maintains VPRN integrity by enabling RR VPN forwarding to handle route targets appropriately

The solution ensures BGP will use the lowest-preference OSPFv3 instance's segment routing tunnels for next-hop resolution while preserving existing VPRN service functionality.
