To implement TTL-based filtering for BGP sessions with your peering partner at AS 12345, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-IP>
            ttl-security 64
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the BGP group containing the peering session and `<neighbor-IP>` with the specific neighbor's IP address. This configuration ensures the router only accepts BGP packets from this peer if their TTL value is 64 or higher. 

For completeness, you may also want to verify that the peering partner is sending packets with an initial TTL of at least 64 (typically achieved by setting `multihop 64` on their side if it's not a direct connection).
