To enforce TTL-based filtering for your BGP peering session with a minimum TTL of 64, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <partner-IP> ttl-security 64
```

If this is an eBGP multi-hop session, ensure the outbound TTL is also set to 64:
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <partner-IP> multihop 64
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<partner-IP>` with the partner router's IP address. This configuration will drop any BGP packets received with a TTL less than 64 while maintaining session stability for valid packets.
