Here are the CLI configuration commands to establish an eBGP session with proper policy controls:

```
configure router bgp
    group <EBGP_GROUP_NAME>
        type external
        neighbor <THIRD_PARTY_ROUTER_IP>
            peer-as <REMOTE_AS_NUMBER>
            multipath ebgp <MAX_PATHS_VALUE>
            third-party-nexthop
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace:
- `<EBGP_GROUP_NAME>` with your desired group name
- `<THIRD_PARTY_ROUTER_IP>` with the neighbor's IP address
- `<REMOTE_AS_NUMBER>` with the third-party router's AS number
- `<MAX_PATHS_VALUE>` with your desired maximum paths (1-64)

For additional policy control, you may want to add import/export policies after the `neighbor` configuration.
