Here are the CLI configuration commands to ensure proper recursive next-hop resolution for both labeled and unlabeled IPv4/IPv6 prefixes using BGP-learned routes:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            # Enable BGP route usage for unlabeled IPv4/IPv6 next-hop resolution
            use-bgp-routes
            
            # Configure shortcut tunnels for unlabeled routes
            shortcut-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        bgp
                        sr-policy
                exit
                family ipv6
                    resolution-filter
                        bgp
                        sr-policy
                exit
            exit
            
            # Configure transport tunnels for labeled routes
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family label-ipv4
                        resolution-filter
                            bgp
                            sr-policy
                    exit
                    family label-ipv6
                        resolution-filter
                            bgp
                            sr-policy
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables BGP route usage for recursive next-hop resolution
2. Configures both BGP and SR-Policy as resolution methods for:
   - Unlabeled IPv4/IPv6 routes via shortcut tunnels
   - Labeled IPv4/IPv6 routes via transport tunnels
