To ensure proper recursive resolution of next-hops for both IPv4 and IPv6 prefixes without explicit labels on a Nokia router acting as a BGP route reflector, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp next-hop-res
    use-bgp-routes
exit
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes
    rr-use-route-table
    transport-tunnel family label-ipv4
        resolution-filter bgp
    exit
    transport-tunnel family label-ipv6
        resolution-filter bgp
    exit
exit
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunnel family ipv4
    resolution-filter bgp
exit
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunnel family ipv6
    resolution-filter bgp
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables BGP route recursion for next-hop resolution
2. Allows the route reflector to use the route table for resolving labeled routes
3. Configures BGP tunneling for both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled routes
4. Sets up shortcut tunnel resolution for unlabeled IPv4 and IPv6 routes
