To properly verify and ensure the 'redirect-to-IPv4' action is correctly enforced for propagated flowspec rules, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp flowspec
    validate-redirect-ip
exit
```

This will enable validation of the `redirect-to-IPv4` action for received flowspec IPv4 routes. The default behavior is `no validate-redirect-ip`, so explicitly enabling this ensures proper enforcement of the redirect action.

For additional validation of destination prefixes in flowspec rules, you may also want to enable:
```
configure router bgp flowspec
    validate-dest-prefix
exit
```
