To extend your existing BGP import route policies to cover EVPN NLRI while maintaining consistent traffic engineering across both underlay and overlay, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    vpn-apply-import
exit
```

If you need to apply specific import policies for EVPN routes at the group or neighbor level, configure them explicitly:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    import <existing-policy-name>
    def-recv-evpn-encap vxlan
exit
```

For SR-based traffic engineering in the underlay, ensure proper next-hop resolution with:

```cli
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunn family ipv4 resolution-filter
    sr-policy
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Apply your base BGP import policies to EVPN routes via `vpn-apply-import`
2. Maintain VXLAN encapsulation consistency for EVPN routes
3. Preserve SR-based traffic engineering capabilities for underlay routes
