Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure your Nokia 7750 SR PE router to propagate up to eight distinct VPN-IPv4 route advertisements to neighboring Route Reflectors (RRs) while preventing inbound acceptance of these prefixes, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group RR_GROUP
        family vpn-ipv4
        neighbor <RR_IP_ADDRESS>
            add-paths
                vpn-ipv4 send 8 receive none
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<RR_IP_ADDRESS>` with the actual IP address of your Route Reflector. This configuration:
1. Enables sending up to 8 VPN-IPv4 paths to the specified RR
2. Explicitly disables receiving multiple paths from the RR (`receive none`)
3. Maintains this behavior specifically for VPN-IPv4 routes within the BGP session

For additional protection against unwanted route acceptance, you may also want to apply inbound route policies to filter VPN-IPv4 prefixes at the neighbor level.
