Here's the optimal BGP policy configuration to propagate up to eight distinct VPN-IPv6 prefixes while blocking external VPNv6 routes:

```
configure router bgp
    group <your_pe_group_name>
        family vpn-ipv6
        neighbor <peer_ip_address>
            advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv6
            vpn-apply-import
            exit
        exit
    add-paths
        vpn-ipv6 send 8 receive none
        exit
    no shutdown
exit
```

Key elements of this configuration:
1. Enables VPN-IPv6 address family for the peer group
2. Advertises IPv6 next hops for VPN-IPv6 routes
3. Applies base BGP import policies to VPN routes
4. Allows sending up to 8 VPN-IPv6 prefixes (via add-paths)
5. Explicitly blocks receiving external VPNv6 routes ("receive none")
6. Maintains MPLS forwarding through standard operation

For additional security, you should create specific import/export policies to further control route propagation if needed.
